title:    Thirty minutes later, with nobody touching anything
subtitle: Measured, not assumed. Poll every ~14s across the expiry boundary.
width:    980
---
# Grant approved  22:31:54Z      requestedDuration 1800s
# Documented expiry  23:01:54Z   (approval + 1800s)

  23:01:20Z  still bound: roles/iam.securityReviewer
  23:01:34Z  still bound: roles/iam.securityReviewer
  23:01:48Z  still bound: roles/iam.securityReviewer     <- 6s BEFORE expiry
  23:02:01Z  GONE                                        <- 7s AFTER expiry

# Removal happened inside that 13-second window. No cleanup job, no
# terraform destroy, no human. The binding left the policy on its own.

$ gcloud pam grants list ... --format="value(state)"
ENDED

$ gcloud resource-manager folders get-iam-policy folders/<FOLDER> \
    --impersonate-service-account=jit-access-demo@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com

ERROR: (gcloud.resource-manager.folders.get-iam-policy)
  [jit-access-demo@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com] does not have permission
  to access folders instance [<FOLDER>:getIamPolicy] (or it may not exist):
  The caller does not have permission.

# Identical to figure 01. That is the whole week: the denial came back
# without anybody bringing it back.
